WEBVTT

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:38.705
Delivery boy Philip J. Fry,
reporting for duty.

00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:41.208
Dr. Zoidberg, soaking in brine.

00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:48.006
What is the meaning of this?

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.259
We've got a delivery, people.
Let's move, let's move.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.053
Amy, mission profile.

00:00:55.556 --> 00:00:56.723
Interesting.

00:00:56.849 --> 00:00:58.559
Interesting.

00:00:58.642 --> 00:01:00.310
Dr. Zoidberg, mission bag?

00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:01.770
Packed and ready, sir.

00:01:02.563 --> 00:01:03.814
What's this?

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.566
This is the same toy surprise
I got last time.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.527
I can't work under these conditions.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.696
And without me, there is no mission.

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.030
I am the mission.

00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:13.574
We're back from the mission.

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.701
Wha... You went without me?

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:18.287
You were looking up curse words
in the dictionary.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.789
It seemed like a better use of your time.

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:23.375
But... But I'm the delivery boy.

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.627
Don't worry, everything went fine.

00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:26.962
Better than usual.

00:01:27.045 --> 00:01:28.589
We got medals.

00:01:29.006 --> 00:01:30.048
Good work, team.

00:01:30.132 --> 00:01:32.134
We really pulled together on this one.

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:33.302
Whoo-hoo!

00:01:34.845 --> 00:01:36.346
They got medals.

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:47.441
I'm real sorry I missed the mission.

00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:49.610
I wasn't there
and you might have needed me.

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:50.694
Nope.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.696
- But if I had been there...
- Nope.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.031
- Li...
- Nope.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.324
- Bender's great.
- Nope.

00:01:56.575 --> 00:01:59.745
Listen, Leela, let me make it up
by taking you out for dinner tonight.

00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:00.829
Nope.

00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:02.414
I've got a date with Chaz.

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:03.707
Chaz?

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.959
I met him at that
charity cockfight last week.

00:02:06.043 --> 00:02:07.461
He's the mayor's aide.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:08.921
Ooh, you go, mutant girl.

00:02:09.004 --> 00:02:10.005
Ooh!

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.424
I do go. He's a very important man.

00:02:12.508 --> 00:02:14.593
So? I'm just as important as him.

00:02:17.054 --> 00:02:19.264
It's just that,
the kind of importance I have,

00:02:19.348 --> 00:02:21.183
it doesn't matter if I don't do it.

00:02:29.942 --> 00:02:32.069
I'm nobody.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.613
There are guys in the background
of Mary Worth comics

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:36.031
who are more important than me.

00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:37.741
Aw, buck up, meatloaf.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.618
Bender will take you out tonight
and cheer you up.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.828
What do you want to do?
And I mean anything.

00:02:41.912 --> 00:02:43.121
You have the power.

00:02:43.205 --> 00:02:44.623
Name it and I'm there.

00:02:44.706 --> 00:02:45.958
You the man.

00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:47.376
Well, okay.

00:02:47.459 --> 00:02:48.544
Let's go bowling.

00:02:48.627 --> 00:02:50.212
Nah.

00:02:55.884 --> 00:02:56.927
Table for two?

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.136
Step right this way.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.888
I'm afraid we don't have a reservation

00:02:59.972 --> 00:03:02.724
but, um, as you can see,
I'm the mayor's aide.

00:03:02.808 --> 00:03:04.184
Table for two, please.

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:06.436
Okay, then.

00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:16.572
Bam!

00:03:16.655 --> 00:03:17.990
It's okay, my man.

00:03:18.073 --> 00:03:20.826
I got you covered
on your next health inspection.

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:23.579
Aw, I really appreciate that,
Mr. Mayor's aide.

00:03:23.662 --> 00:03:24.997
Here you go.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.790
Compliments of the house.

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.918
Wow, free bread at a restaurant.

00:03:30.002 --> 00:03:31.962
Is there anything you can't do?

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.755
I can't fail the mayor.

00:03:33.839 --> 00:03:35.299
Not ever.

00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:36.717
Oh...

00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:48.478
Oh, geez, better not let Leela see me.

00:03:48.562 --> 00:03:50.439
Hey, I hear Fry.

00:03:50.981 --> 00:03:52.608
Boy, am I glad you're here.

00:03:52.691 --> 00:03:55.360
You are? So things aren't working out
with what's-his-name?

00:03:55.444 --> 00:03:57.613
Actually, they are.

00:03:57.696 --> 00:04:01.033
Confidentially, I might not make it back
to my apartment tonight.

00:04:01.116 --> 00:04:02.743
Could you walk Nibbler for me?

00:04:04.912 --> 00:04:07.247
And bring a baggie
in case he drops a steamer.

00:04:07.331 --> 00:04:08.749
Have a great night.

00:04:13.795 --> 00:04:16.256
Oh, no, please, no...

00:04:17.841 --> 00:04:19.009
Oh, perfect.

00:04:28.435 --> 00:04:31.313
Whoa-ho-ho,
smells like a 2-8-9 in progress.

00:04:31.396 --> 00:04:32.814
Failure to scoop.

00:04:32.898 --> 00:04:34.441
Aw, yeah.

00:04:35.943 --> 00:04:37.277
Wait, I'm trying.

00:04:37.361 --> 00:04:39.071
It weighs as much as a thousand suns.

00:04:44.034 --> 00:04:45.118
Don't worry, Fry.

00:04:45.202 --> 00:04:48.247
I'll pull some strings, see if
I can't get you tried as a juvenile.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.581
Oh, Chaz.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.218
I'm as worthless as this trash can.

00:05:03.178 --> 00:05:05.180
You think
I'm as worthless as you?

00:05:05.264 --> 00:05:06.974
Try catching garbage in your head

00:05:07.057 --> 00:05:09.184
and raising six kids, you dumb townie.

00:05:14.857 --> 00:05:17.985
Oh, Nibbler,
at least I'm important to you.

00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:20.237
Even if it's only
'cause I clean up your poop.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.074
The poop eradication is but
one aspect of your importance.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:29.955
Did you just talk?

00:05:30.122 --> 00:05:31.123
Indeed.

00:05:31.206 --> 00:05:33.584
And I have other amazing powers as well.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.252
Like what?

00:05:47.264 --> 00:05:48.765
Are you my mommy?

00:05:48.849 --> 00:05:49.850
Negative.

00:05:51.393 --> 00:05:52.561
Ooh...

00:06:09.453 --> 00:06:10.913
Welcome, Lord Nibbler.

00:06:10.996 --> 00:06:12.247
Welcome acknowledged.

00:06:12.331 --> 00:06:15.334
I bring with me the Mighty One.

00:06:16.585 --> 00:06:17.586
Huh?

00:06:17.719 --> 00:06:22.349
At last, our centuries upon centuries
of waiting have achieved fruition.

00:06:22.432 --> 00:06:25.227
Aw, aren't you a fuzzy wittle guy.

00:06:27.396 --> 00:06:28.605
Stop that!

00:06:28.689 --> 00:06:29.690
Uh, please.

00:06:29.773 --> 00:06:30.857
Your Mightiness.

00:06:30.941 --> 00:06:32.526
Mightiness? Are you off your nut?

00:06:32.609 --> 00:06:34.945
I just got kidnapped
by a bunch of guinea pigs.

00:06:37.781 --> 00:06:40.033
- Does he not know?
- He does not know.

00:06:40.117 --> 00:06:42.327
- He knows not?
- Knows not does he.

00:06:42.411 --> 00:06:44.121
- Not he knows...
- Enough!

00:06:44.204 --> 00:06:46.790
Fry, it is my duty to inform you

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:49.334
that the fate of humanity,
the fate of our race,

00:06:49.418 --> 00:06:53.130
indeed, the fate of all that
exists and ever will exist

00:06:53.213 --> 00:06:54.590
rests with you.

00:06:55.048 --> 00:06:58.844
You are the single most important person
in the universe.

00:07:00.721 --> 00:07:02.222
Oh, snap.

00:07:07.603 --> 00:07:10.022
On this auspicious occasion,

00:07:10.105 --> 00:07:13.942
let the Horn of Eternity
cut a thunderous blast.

00:07:19.698 --> 00:07:22.534
The feast of a thousand beasts is begun.

00:07:29.291 --> 00:07:31.627
- You gonna eat that?
- Maybe later.

00:07:34.004 --> 00:07:37.424
The time has come to discuss matters
of the gravest importance.

00:07:39.301 --> 00:07:41.261
Fry, do you remember some months ago

00:07:41.345 --> 00:07:43.597
when Earth was attacked by flying brains?

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.558
Hmm... I remember
the square-dancing stomachs,

00:07:46.642 --> 00:07:48.727
although that might have been
a Mylanta commercial.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:51.021
Wait, the brains! I do remember.

00:07:51.104 --> 00:07:53.357
But no one else does.
They said I was crazy.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:54.441
On the contrary.

00:07:54.524 --> 00:07:56.818
You remember because
you were the only one immune

00:07:56.902 --> 00:07:58.320
to the brains' mental attack.

00:07:58.403 --> 00:07:59.571
Because I'm so smart?

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:03.408
Oh, my.

00:08:03.492 --> 00:08:05.953
Anyway, your immunity is due to the fact

00:08:06.036 --> 00:08:07.788
that you lack the delta brain wave.

00:08:10.207 --> 00:08:12.501
It's a genetic abnormality which resulted

00:08:12.584 --> 00:08:15.337
when you went back in time
and performed certain actions

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.714
which made you your own grandfather.

00:08:18.006 --> 00:08:19.967
I did do the nasty in the past-y.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:21.134
Verily.

00:08:21.218 --> 00:08:24.930
And that past-nastification
is what shields you from the brains.

00:08:25.013 --> 00:08:28.141
You are the last hope of the universe.

00:08:28.225 --> 00:08:29.685
So I really am important?

00:08:29.768 --> 00:08:31.436
How I feel when I'm drunk is correct?

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:32.604
Yes.

00:08:32.688 --> 00:08:35.524
Except, the Dave Matthews Band
doesn't rock.

00:08:40.529 --> 00:08:42.197
For a thousand years,

00:08:42.281 --> 00:08:45.325
the evil brains have been
constructing the "Info-Sphere,"

00:08:45.409 --> 00:08:49.705
a giant memory bank twice the size
of three ordinary memory banks.

00:08:49.788 --> 00:08:51.290
What's so evil about that?

00:08:51.373 --> 00:08:53.834
They plan to collect
all the information in the universe

00:08:53.917 --> 00:08:55.752
and store it within the sphere.

00:08:55.836 --> 00:08:57.754
- So they're trying to learn things?
- Right.

00:08:57.838 --> 00:08:59.131
Those bastards!

00:08:59.214 --> 00:09:02.259
Being brains, they feel compelled
to know everything.

00:09:02.342 --> 00:09:03.927
And soon they will.

00:09:04.011 --> 00:09:05.679
I'm as mad as I've ever been!

00:09:05.846 --> 00:09:07.389
Once their task is complete,

00:09:07.472 --> 00:09:10.225
they will ensure that
no new information arises

00:09:10.309 --> 00:09:12.060
in the only way possible,

00:09:12.144 --> 00:09:13.896
by destroying the universe.

00:09:14.187 --> 00:09:15.981
Now it's personal.

00:09:16.231 --> 00:09:18.734
Your mission is to infiltrate
the Info-Sphere

00:09:18.817 --> 00:09:21.111
and plant this Quantum Interphase Bomb,

00:09:21.194 --> 00:09:23.322
blasting them into an alternate universe

00:09:23.405 --> 00:09:25.324
from which there is no return.

00:09:25.407 --> 00:09:28.827
Then, outrun the blast
on this Scooty-Puff, Jr.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.880
Okay, let's go through this
once more from the start...

00:09:49.181 --> 00:09:50.390
Brains!

00:09:50.474 --> 00:09:51.767
Fear not, Mighty One.

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:54.353
Your missing brain wave
makes you invisible to them

00:09:54.436 --> 00:09:56.605
so long as you avoid intense thinking.

00:09:56.688 --> 00:09:57.731
Sorry, what?

00:09:57.814 --> 00:09:59.066
I wasn't paying attention.

00:09:59.149 --> 00:10:01.026
- That is most wise.
- Who?

00:10:05.197 --> 00:10:07.908
In a few seconds,
the brains will finish scanning

00:10:07.991 --> 00:10:10.244
the last bits of information
in the universe.

00:10:10.327 --> 00:10:11.995
"Beavers mate for life."

00:10:12.079 --> 00:10:13.664
"Eleven greater than four."

00:10:13.747 --> 00:10:16.708
"For quality carpets,
visit Kaplan's Carpet Warehouse."

00:10:19.586 --> 00:10:22.464
Now the Info-Sphere will open
its protective crust

00:10:22.547 --> 00:10:24.341
so as to scan itself,

00:10:24.424 --> 00:10:26.635
completing its thousand-year task.

00:10:37.437 --> 00:10:39.815
This is your one chance
to enter the Sphere.

00:10:39.898 --> 00:10:41.608
Scoot! Scoot now!

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:09.636
I'm at the input console.

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:12.306
I'm a little nervous,
and I've got brain in my butt crack.

00:11:12.389 --> 00:11:13.557
Roger.

00:11:14.349 --> 00:11:15.809
Once you press the detonator,

00:11:15.893 --> 00:11:18.604
you will have 60 seconds
for an exciting escape.

00:11:22.774 --> 00:11:23.775
Hey, wait.

00:11:23.859 --> 00:11:25.777
This brain knows everything
about everything, right?

00:11:25.861 --> 00:11:27.195
It will soon.

00:11:27.279 --> 00:11:29.615
That's why you're supposed
to be setting off a bomb.

00:11:29.698 --> 00:11:30.741
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:30.824 --> 00:11:32.409
But I can't pass up a chance
to learn the answers

00:11:32.492 --> 00:11:34.411
to the greatest questions of all time.

00:11:35.704 --> 00:11:37.831
Is it true that postage stamp
glue is made of...

00:11:37.915 --> 00:11:39.917
Correct. Toad mucus!

00:11:41.293 --> 00:11:43.754
There's no time for this.
Activate the bomb.

00:11:43.837 --> 00:11:45.088
Wait, wait, wait.

00:11:45.172 --> 00:11:47.132
What really killed the dinosaurs?

00:11:47.257 --> 00:11:48.550
Me!

00:11:50.552 --> 00:11:52.596
Unauthorized data access.

00:11:59.061 --> 00:12:00.062
Uh-oh.

00:12:01.396 --> 00:12:04.358
Detecting trace amounts
of mental activity.

00:12:04.441 --> 00:12:07.527
Possibly a dead weasel
or a cartoon viewer.

00:12:09.238 --> 00:12:11.531
Ew, gross. Cut it out.

00:12:11.615 --> 00:12:14.701
Odd. He is immune to our psionic attack.

00:12:14.785 --> 00:12:17.913
Impossible. We're an ambitious young squad
with everything to prove.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:22.000
It appears we are in
the presence of the fabled one.

00:12:22.084 --> 00:12:25.379
But without his Scooty-Puff, Jr.,
he cannot escape.

00:12:27.631 --> 00:12:28.632
Huh?

00:12:28.715 --> 00:12:30.217
A Quantum Interface Bomb?

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:31.552
Are you insane in the membrane?

00:12:31.635 --> 00:12:33.470
You got it, Poindexter.

00:12:39.351 --> 00:12:40.352
Not good!

00:12:40.435 --> 00:12:43.981
Detonation in T-minus 60 Earth seconds.

00:12:46.275 --> 00:12:47.317
You fool!

00:12:47.401 --> 00:12:49.820
You'll be transported
to the other universe with us,

00:12:49.903 --> 00:12:51.572
trapped there for all eternity!

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:54.616
And we'll form a tightly-knit clique
that you won't be part of.

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.869
Well, at least I did one
important thing with my life.

00:12:57.953 --> 00:13:00.038
Leading good to victory over evil!

00:13:00.163 --> 00:13:01.206
- Hurray!
- Yeah!

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:02.291
Exactly!

00:13:02.416 --> 00:13:04.418
The Nibblonians, good?

00:13:04.501 --> 00:13:08.005
Ha! During your last moments
in this universe,

00:13:08.088 --> 00:13:10.215
perhaps you should query our database

00:13:10.299 --> 00:13:14.011
concerning the night of December 31, 1999.

00:13:14.094 --> 00:13:16.138
The day I got frozen? What about it?

00:13:16.221 --> 00:13:18.432
No. Uh, don't ask about that.

00:13:18.515 --> 00:13:20.392
It would be, uh, boring.

00:13:20.475 --> 00:13:21.476
Ah, forget it, then.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.104
- Query!
- Okay. Sheesh.

00:13:24.187 --> 00:13:29.318
What happened to me, Philip J. Fry,
on the night of December 31, 1999?

00:13:29.401 --> 00:13:30.986
Clarification request.

00:13:31.069 --> 00:13:33.113
Are you the Philip J. Fry from Earth

00:13:33.196 --> 00:13:36.450
or the Philip J. Fry from
Hovering Squid World 97-A?

00:13:36.533 --> 00:13:38.535
Earth, you fat idiot. Hurry up.

00:13:44.541 --> 00:13:45.542
Hello?

00:13:45.626 --> 00:13:48.003
Pizza delivery for, uh...

00:13:50.088 --> 00:13:51.465
Oh, crud.

00:13:51.548 --> 00:13:54.176
Ugh, I can't believe how fat I look.

00:13:58.388 --> 00:14:00.057
Aah, Nibbler's there.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:01.141
Wait, what!

00:14:06.355 --> 00:14:07.773
What the...

00:14:09.608 --> 00:14:11.777
I... I don't understand.

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:13.987
You made me go in the freezer tube?

00:14:14.071 --> 00:14:17.199
Detonation in T-minus 15 seconds.

00:14:17.282 --> 00:14:18.742
You little runts froze me.

00:14:18.825 --> 00:14:20.118
You took away my life.

00:14:20.202 --> 00:14:21.245
We can explain.

00:14:21.328 --> 00:14:23.705
No, you can't! Shut your adorable trap!

00:14:23.789 --> 00:14:24.998
We had no choice.

00:14:25.082 --> 00:14:27.334
You were the only one who could help us.

00:14:27.417 --> 00:14:31.380
What is one life
weighedagainst the entire universe?

00:14:31.922 --> 00:14:34.216
But it was my life.

00:14:34.675 --> 00:14:37.928
Detonation in two, one...

00:14:38.011 --> 00:14:40.180
Will the owner
of a white Pontiac Firebird...

00:14:40.264 --> 00:14:41.807
Oh, never mind. Zero!

00:14:58.699 --> 00:15:00.325
Well, here we are.

00:15:00.409 --> 00:15:01.785
Trapped for eternity.

00:15:01.868 --> 00:15:03.620
We could sing American Pie.

00:15:03.704 --> 00:15:06.331
Go ahead. I deserve it.

00:15:06.415 --> 00:15:09.626
I wish those stupid raccoons had
never brought me to the future.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:12.629
I have shocking data relevant
to this conversation!

00:15:12.713 --> 00:15:15.465
We don't care, you dope.
We're in another universe.

00:15:15.549 --> 00:15:16.884
You're not in charge anymore.

00:15:16.967 --> 00:15:19.136
It is possible for the Philip Fry

00:15:19.219 --> 00:15:22.598
to resume his life on December 31, 1999.

00:15:22.681 --> 00:15:24.600
Really? I can go back in time?

00:15:26.018 --> 00:15:27.936
There is a nexus point between universes

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:30.772
at the space-time where you
entered the cryogenic tube.

00:15:30.856 --> 00:15:33.442
You, and only you, can return there.

00:15:33.525 --> 00:15:35.068
Interesting.

00:15:35.152 --> 00:15:38.989
You could stop the Nibblonian
from pushing you into the cryogenic tube.

00:15:39.072 --> 00:15:40.657
That is interesting.

00:15:40.741 --> 00:15:41.825
Why?

00:15:41.909 --> 00:15:44.411
It will be as if you never came
to the future.

00:15:44.494 --> 00:15:48.165
You will have your life back,
and we will succeed in our plan

00:15:48.248 --> 00:15:50.751
to understand and destroy the universe.

00:15:50.834 --> 00:15:52.252
Everybody wins.

00:15:52.336 --> 00:15:54.546
The human will be returned to the past.

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:56.089
Meanwhile...

00:15:56.632 --> 00:15:58.800
I love rocket skating.

00:15:58.884 --> 00:16:01.136
But the wait is always so long.

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:04.806
Poor Fry once stood on line six hours
just to get me a ticket.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:08.477
Six hours? Pfft.
Sounds like a real nobody.

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:13.148
But now it's time for somebody,
and some chick he's with, to go skating.

00:16:16.235 --> 00:16:17.945
You reserved the whole rink?

00:16:18.028 --> 00:16:21.281
Yep. Buzzed ahead,
let them know whose aide was coming by.

00:16:21.365 --> 00:16:23.116
The mayor's, that's whose.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:24.576
Oh, Chaz!

00:16:25.327 --> 00:16:26.578
Mm...

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:37.130
Mr. Vogel? I thought we was going skating.

00:16:37.214 --> 00:16:39.341
No, we're not important enough.

00:16:39.424 --> 00:16:40.926
Everybody just hold hands

00:16:41.009 --> 00:16:43.136
until the bus driver
comes back from his haircut.

00:16:44.012 --> 00:16:47.015
Aw, let's let those kids skate with us.

00:16:47.099 --> 00:16:48.809
What, seriously?

00:16:48.892 --> 00:16:50.310
I'm trying to impress you
with my clout here.

00:16:50.394 --> 00:16:52.312
I know, and it's working.

00:16:52.396 --> 00:16:54.982
But think how much
skating would mean to those kids.

00:16:55.065 --> 00:16:57.568
We came here instead of eating today.

00:16:57.651 --> 00:17:01.196
This might be their only chance
to skate here their whole lives.

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:02.656
Who are we to say they can't?

00:17:02.739 --> 00:17:05.492
The mayor's aide, and this badge.

00:17:05.576 --> 00:17:06.743
Beat it, kids!

00:17:06.827 --> 00:17:08.579
Come back when you got connections!

00:17:10.539 --> 00:17:11.707
All right, little ones.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.208
Back to the Orphanarium.

00:17:13.292 --> 00:17:15.460
You can slide around
the gym in your socks.

00:17:15.544 --> 00:17:17.004
What socks?

00:17:17.421 --> 00:17:20.465
So, am I going
to get lucky tonight, or what?

00:17:29.683 --> 00:17:31.894
I hope your calculations are correct.

00:17:32.019 --> 00:17:36.064
Our calculations are always correct,
for we are gigantic brains.

00:17:36.148 --> 00:17:38.066
Initiate space-time transfer.

00:17:53.248 --> 00:17:56.376
I hereby place an order
for one cheese pizza.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:59.129
One pie, nothing good on it. Name?

00:17:59.212 --> 00:18:01.632
I, period, C, period, Wiener.

00:18:03.175 --> 00:18:04.676
Uh, talk a little louder.

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:07.429
It sounds like you got some kind
of tiny head on you or something.

00:18:17.606 --> 00:18:18.774
Hello?

00:18:18.857 --> 00:18:20.859
Pizza delivery for, uh...

00:18:20.943 --> 00:18:22.402
"I.C. Wiener"?

00:18:23.028 --> 00:18:24.363
Oh, crud.

00:18:25.822 --> 00:18:27.699
Gotcha!

00:18:28.492 --> 00:18:29.660
I don't understand.

00:18:29.743 --> 00:18:30.786
Yes, you do.

00:18:30.869 --> 00:18:33.288
You came back in time
to knock me into that freezer,

00:18:33.372 --> 00:18:35.207
and now I came back in time to stop you.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:37.000
I did not come back in time.

00:18:37.084 --> 00:18:38.669
My people lack that ability.

00:18:38.752 --> 00:18:40.545
But I know you in the future.

00:18:40.629 --> 00:18:41.713
I cleaned your poop.

00:18:41.797 --> 00:18:43.090
Quite possible.

00:18:43.173 --> 00:18:45.676
We live long and are celebrated poopers.

00:18:45.759 --> 00:18:48.095
You will meet me
when I'm a thousand years older.

00:18:48.178 --> 00:18:49.972
Not if you don't freeze me.

00:18:52.891 --> 00:18:56.353
Please. Our sages foresee
that in a thousand years,

00:18:56.436 --> 00:18:59.856
for one moment, the fate
of the universe will depend on you.

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:04.403
Since you will not live that long,
I must freeze you now.

00:19:04.486 --> 00:19:06.113
Well, why couldn't you just ask me?

00:19:06.196 --> 00:19:07.906
We were afraid you would refuse.

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:10.117
Of course not. I love the future.

00:19:11.535 --> 00:19:13.412
Then why are you choking me right now?

00:19:13.495 --> 00:19:16.331
Because I don't like being used.

00:19:16.999 --> 00:19:18.792
Well, now it's your choice.

00:19:19.209 --> 00:19:21.253
Is there nothing in the future
worth saving?

00:19:21.336 --> 00:19:23.297
Hmm... Leela.

00:19:23.547 --> 00:19:25.382
But she doesn't think much of me.

00:19:25.465 --> 00:19:28.010
Ah, she must be the Other.

00:19:28.093 --> 00:19:29.303
The... Wha...

00:19:31.138 --> 00:19:32.806
You must not give up on her.

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:36.560
I am stationed on a distant world
known as Vergon 6,

00:19:36.643 --> 00:19:38.437
but if you return to the future,

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:41.565
I will transfer to Earth
to give you what help I can.

00:19:43.025 --> 00:19:44.443
Ten...

00:19:44.526 --> 00:19:47.529
You really think I would've
had a chance with Leela?

00:19:47.613 --> 00:19:49.364
- You must choose.
- ...seven, six...

00:19:49.448 --> 00:19:51.241
The present or the future.

00:19:51.408 --> 00:19:54.369
To save yourself or save Leela.

00:19:54.453 --> 00:19:55.537
...two, one.

00:20:04.588 --> 00:20:06.590
Yes! Here I come, future.

00:20:06.673 --> 00:20:07.883
Oh, no. Wait!

00:20:07.966 --> 00:20:10.427
I'm going to get trapped
in the Info-Sphere again.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:14.056
Just remember
that Scooty-Puff, Jr. sucks...

00:20:16.225 --> 00:20:18.727
In a thousand years, I'll get right on it.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:21.188
And so, a thousand years later,

00:20:21.271 --> 00:20:24.316
Fry once again infiltrated the Info-Sphere

00:20:24.399 --> 00:20:26.902
and set off his amazing bomb.

00:20:26.985 --> 00:20:28.904
Only this time...

00:20:44.586 --> 00:20:47.297
Thank you for saving the universe, Fry.

00:20:47.881 --> 00:20:48.882
Here.

00:20:48.966 --> 00:20:52.261
Wow, thanks.
If you ever need a savior again, just ask.

00:20:52.928 --> 00:20:55.097
Oh, we will.

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:56.515
We will.

00:20:59.685 --> 00:21:02.271
Man, I can't wait to tell
everyone what happened.

00:21:02.354 --> 00:21:05.732
Yes. Incidentally,
I need to remain undercover

00:21:05.816 --> 00:21:07.776
so I'm blanking your memory.

00:21:10.779 --> 00:21:13.991
Huh. Did everything just taste purple
for a second?

00:21:14.074 --> 00:21:17.160
Oh, well. Let's go home,
you dumb poop machine.

00:21:22.249 --> 00:21:24.167
Bender, would you do the honors?

00:21:24.251 --> 00:21:25.335
With gusto.

00:21:31.425 --> 00:21:32.467
Hey, Leela.

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:34.595
I guess I got this for you.

00:21:34.678 --> 00:21:36.597
Oh. Thank you.

00:21:38.098 --> 00:21:39.266
You know what, Fry?

00:21:39.349 --> 00:21:42.561
I don't care if you're not
the most important person in the universe.

00:21:42.644 --> 00:21:45.397
It really makes me happy
to see you right now.

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:48.483
Then I am the most important person
in the universe.

00:21:54.156 --> 00:21:55.365
Yes!